{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 42, :comments ["The reason for <b>\"These are the families of Dan according to their families\"</b>: for the descendants of Shuham made families that were called by the name of the head of the family, but they were all traced back to Shuham the chief, and were named after him by his name — as you might say: for Daniel, the family of Daniel the Shuhami; for Ezekiel, the family of Ezekiel the Shuhami. Now they are many families, yet a single family with regard to the Shuhami, and therefore he traces all of them back to him. And according to the opinion of those who say that they are traced back to those who went down to Egypt, there were many families called by the names of their fathers who were born in Egypt, but here he traces them only to the Shuhami, because he alone went down to Egypt."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:08:50.108117794Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}